It's obvious play rates and times vary greatly. I'm
astounded when someone talks about getting to minetown in 15
minutes. That's probably 6 hours for me. I don't enter the
annual tournament because I've never finished an ascension
in less than 2 months (there have been 12). My ascensions
have taken from 40K to 65K turns. The calendar time is
because I have a lot of demands for my time: job, wife, dog,
kids, grand kids, bowling league, church, video games, other
computer games, bridge tournaments, golf, reading and a
couple of hours of TV every week. 

I would be surprised if my keyboard time was less than the
32 hours that Janis estimated. There are roughly 75 levels
to complete, 30 minutes each would be fast for me, I'm not
even sure 1 hour each would cover it. Your 15 hours would
have you completing a level every 12 minutes. I spend longer
than that reviewing where the game stands when I restart. I
spend a lot of time thinking, naming, checking, making
notes, managing inventory, etc. But, it only took 12 games
total for the last four classes I ascended and some of those
included conducts. My overall success rate for 3.4.x is 23%.
